/* ADD A TIME ZONE - no C knowledge needed, and you never touch a .c/.h file.
 *
 * Add a line: X("the zone's name", "its POSIX TZ string").
 *
 *   - The name is what users type in SET TZ, such as "America/New_York".
 *     The part after the slash also works alone: SET TZ NEW_YORK.
 *   - The TZ string says how far the zone is from UTC and when its summer
 *     time starts and ends: "EST5EDT,M3.2.0/2,M11.1.0/2" is EST, 5 hours
 *     west of UTC, with EDT an hour ahead of it from 2:00 on the second
 *     Sunday of March to 2:00 on the first Sunday of November. A zone east
 *     of UTC has a minus: "JST-9".
 *   - HELP SET TZ shows the zones in the order they are here.
 *
 * Build and test with SET TZ <name> and STATUS.
 */

X("Etc/UTC", "UTC0")
X("Africa/Accra", "GMT0")
X("Africa/Algiers", "CET-1")
X("Africa/Cairo", "EET-2")
X("Africa/Casablanca", "WET-1")
X("Africa/Johannesburg", "SAST-2")
X("Africa/Lagos", "WAT-1")
X("Africa/Nairobi", "EAT-3")
